    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e42f9f4e_df32c9e8",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 3637,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T23:10:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The effect of setting this flag is to trigger a GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS message. I understand there may have been synchronization issues with the PPM and the PDM in terms of the PPM knowing when the PDM had reached a steady state. But, it\u0027s not clear to me why the cached info from the most recent GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS would still not be the most recent and up to date information.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3637,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 3637,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "dd97de63d254091d3423237b20d29c554cada36b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71370de3_e7d91dd4",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 3637,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T23:25:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UCSI spec says that if the host triggers`SET_PDR`, the resulting swap will not generate connector status change events. Thus any commands with side effects must trigger a GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS manually (simulating a change indication).",
      "parentUuid": "e42f9f4e_df32c9e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3637,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 3637,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "dd97de63d254091d3423237b20d29c554cada36b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "edd9add5_97cb5f98",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 3640,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T22:25:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I\u0027m emitting this event at the right place but it at least queues GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS as part of the execution that emits this event.\n\nIt may be more correct to call this before calling `run_queued_commands` but I\u0027m not 100% sure.",
      "revId": "dd97de63d254091d3423237b20d29c554cada36b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e2e7171_51278285",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 3640,
      "author": {
        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T23:36:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s tricky... the `run_*_policies()` functions can continue to adjust the port state and also queue up more commands after reaching the *_RUN substate and it might take extra cycles of the SM before it truly settles, depending on what policy flags may be set. A queued public command could further complicate this. \n\nI wonder if a more reliable approach would be to implement something like a debounce counter in `pdc_thread()` --track the state and raise the event once you\u0027ve been in a non-command-processing state for N consecutive cycles. That way the SM can bounce around as much as it wants before settling, subject to a timeout of course.",
      "parentUuid": "edd9add5_97cb5f98",
      "revId": "dd97de63d254091d3423237b20d29c554cada36b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3aedf60_4aec9691",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 3640,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T23:56:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think I need to wait for the public apis but I would like for this to wait until the EC has had a chance to respond with anything that may impact the connector status. The goal is that a subsequent, \"GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS\", has all necessary changes that the OS can act upon it.\n\nFor example, if OS sent pr_swap, we need to wait until the EC is in the PDC_ATTACHED_SNK/SRC state (after querying data) and it has had a chance to apply any policy that can impact connector status. That way, trying to `SET_SINK_PATH` will not fail due to incorrect role.",
      "parentUuid": "1e2e7171_51278285",
      "revId": "dd97de63d254091d3423237b20d29c554cada36b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ]
